//Hair
# Her hair flows from the crown. A lock is described by t, from the crown (0) down to the end of
# the longest hair (1): up to t = 0.14841 it lies on a dome around the head (ha is the angle from the
# crown), below that it falls. hzz(t) is the height, hrx(t) and hry(t) are the half-axes of the ellipse the
# hair lies on at that height: they follow the dome, then keep just clear of the shoulders, capelet, arms, book
# and skirt, so that the locks at her sides lie close to her clothes (fitted by the generator). hu(t) is 0 on the dome and grows to 1
# down the fall. hdw keeps a lock's width steady as the hair spreads.
ha(t)=1.5708*min(1,t/0.14841)
hu(t)=max(0,t-0.14841)/0.85159
hzz(t)=12.15+0.76*cos(ha(t))-8.04381*max(0,t-0.14841)
hrx(t)=0.79*sin(ha(t))+34.44364*max(0,t-0.14841)^2+(-78.57892)*max(0,t-0.17841)^2+58.28854*max(0,t-0.20841)^2+(-20.82871)*max(0,t-0.23841)^2+5.63945*max(0,t-0.26341)^2+11.42743*max(0,t-0.28841)^2+(-42.72672)*max(0,t-0.31341)^2+263.52255*max(0,t-0.33841)^2+(-330.90775)*max(0,t-0.36341)^2+135.04786*max(0,t-0.38841)^2+(-85.41214)*max(0,t-0.41841)^2+34.45212*max(0,t-0.45841)^2+32.56879*max(0,t-0.50841)^2+(-58.07747)*max(0,t-0.57841)^2+131.30142*max(0,t-0.66841)^2+(-185.68396)*max(0,t-0.76841)^2+124.43553*max(0,t-0.86841)^2
hry(t)=0.815*sin(ha(t))+34.54775*max(0,t-0.14841)^2+(-79.34091)*max(0,t-0.17841)^2+61.23874*max(0,t-0.20841)^2+(-31.0099)*max(0,t-0.23841)^2+33.28675*max(0,t-0.26341)^2+(-55.03156)*max(0,t-0.28841)^2+115.86503*max(0,t-0.31341)^2+(-224.02451)*max(0,t-0.33841)^2+453.87648*max(0,t-0.36341)^2+(-707.47222)*max(0,t-0.38841)^2+1003.36205*max(0,t-0.41841)^2+(-930.62498)*max(0,t-0.45841)^2+280.79053*max(0,t-0.50841)^2+68.0106*max(0,t-0.57841)^2+(-31.11962)*max(0,t-0.66841)^2+11.60508*max(0,t-0.76841)^2+(-5.88829)*max(0,t-0.86841)^2
hdw(t)=1.54/(1.54+68.99139*max(0,t-0.14841)^2+(-157.91983)*max(0,t-0.17841)^2+119.52729*max(0,t-0.20841)^2+(-51.83861)*max(0,t-0.23841)^2+38.9262*max(0,t-0.26341)^2+(-43.60413)*max(0,t-0.28841)^2+73.13832*max(0,t-0.31341)^2+39.49804*max(0,t-0.33841)^2+122.96874*max(0,t-0.36341)^2+(-572.42437)*max(0,t-0.38841)^2+917.94991*max(0,t-0.41841)^2+(-896.17286)*max(0,t-0.45841)^2+313.35932*max(0,t-0.50841)^2+9.93314*max(0,t-0.57841)^2+100.1818*max(0,t-0.66841)^2+(-174.07889)*max(0,t-0.76841)^2+118.54724*max(0,t-0.86841)^2)
# Her head is tilted and turned (see the generator); a lock turns with it where it lies on the head and
# hangs straight below. hb(t) is 1 on the head and eases to 0 by t = 0.23841; hs and hk are the sine and
# one minus the cosine of the head's turn times hb, and hm scales the lock with the head where it lies on it.
hb(t)=1-min(1,max(0,(t-0.14841)/0.09))^2*(3-2*min(1,max(0,(t-0.14841)/0.09)))
hs(t)=sin(0.14069*hb(t))
hk(t)=1-cos(0.14069*hb(t))
hm(t)=1-0.18*hb(t)
# A lock is a tube around its own flow line. lpc is the angle of that line around the head: a starting
# angle pb+p0 (0 = straight back, + toward her left) whose part p0 closes up by sg as the hair spreads (sg = 1
# falls straight down, sg = 0 fans out over the shoulders; pb is 0 for the back and pi for the front), a drift dr, and a wave of size am that grows down the
# lock. lrc is how far the line stands off the hair surface: its layer la, and a fifth of the wave, so the wave's
# plane tilts a little off the hair (a quarter turn later, as before, the lock wound like a corkscrew). Across the lock (w runs around it) lwd is
# the half-width and lth the thickness, a crescent lcs with three ridges that is flat underneath. ltp tapers
# the lock toward its end te, and lq runs 0..1 over the last stretch, where the tip turns through three
# quarters of a circle: sideways like a hook, or outward like a scroll.
ltp(t,te)=min(1,max(0,te-t)/0.13)^0.6
lq(t,te)=max(0,1-max(0,te-t)/0.08)
lcs(w)=(0.65*sin(w)+0.35*abs(sin(w)))*(0.78+0.22*cos(2*pi*cos(w)))
# The long hair down the back and over the shoulders has the bangs' ridged crescent, and tapers (ltl)
# into its curled tip, as the chest locks do.
ltl(t,te)=min(1,max(0,te-t)/0.1)^0.7
lpc(t,pb,p0,sg,dr,am,kk,ph)=pb+p0*(1-sg*(1-hdw(t)))+dr*hu(t)+am*hu(t)^1.5*sin(kk*hu(t)+ph)
lrc(t,la,am,kk,ph)=la*min(1,t/0.04)+0.2*am*hu(t)^1.5*sin(kk*hu(t)+ph)
lwd(t,te,hw)=hw*ltp(t,te)*hdw(t)
lth(t,w,te,th)=th*ltp(t,te)*lcs(w)*min(1,t/0.04)
lwl(t,te,hw)=hw*ltl(t,te)*hdw(t)
lts(t,w,te,th)=th*ltl(t,te)*lcs(w)*min(1,t/0.04)
hzg(a)=(2/pi)*asin(0.97*sin(a))
# A dark cap and an inner sheet under the locks, so no gap shows skin. The cap stops higher above her left
# eye and a little higher above her right eye, where the forehead shows between the bangs as on the sheet.
